## DI YAML Schema (minimum required fields)

```yaml
# -- DI-LEO-AI-<NNN> -- <Short title>
# IEC 62304 / ISO 13485 Design Input

- id: "DI-LEO-AI-<NNN>"
  type: "Functional"   # Functional | Safety | Performance | Interface | Usability
  derived_from: []     # User need IDs e.g. ["UN-LEO-AI-001"]
  requirement: >
    <The SHALL statement — what the system must do>
  rationale: >
    <Why this requirement exists; clinical or safety justification>

  machine_spec:
    acceptance_criteria:
      - type: "functional"   # functional | safety | performance
        spec: "<Precise measurable criterion>"
    constraints:
      - type: "safety"
        spec: "<Any hard constraints>"
    dependencies: []   # other DI IDs
    downstream_impacts:
      - "<System area affected>"
    technical_details:
      language: "Python"   # or TypeScript, etc.
      framework: "<service or library name>"
      file_structure:
        - "<relative/path/to/implementation_file>"
      estimated_loc: 0

  verification:
    method: "Test"   # Test | Inspection | Analysis | Demonstration
    phase: "OQ"      # OQ | IQ | PQ
    acceptance: >
      <What constitutes a pass — reference test case count and scenario names>
    test_protocol: "VT-LEO-AI-<NNN>"

  safety_class: "B"   # A | B | C
  risks: []           # R-LEO-AI-* IDs
  tags:
    - "<feature-area>"
```

