## DO YAML Schema (minimum required fields)

```yaml
# -- DO-LEO-AI-<NNN> -- <Short title>
# ISO 13485 / IEC 62304 Design Output

- id: "DO-LEO-AI-<NNN>"
  version: "1.0.0"
  type: "Software_Module"   # Software_Module | Algorithm | Configuration | Schema | API_Contract
  status: "draft"           # draft | approved | superseded

  traceability:
    design_inputs: ["DI-LEO-AI-<NNN>"]
    user_needs: []           # UN-LEO-AI-* IDs
    risks_addressed: []      # R-LEO-AI-* IDs
    verification_tests: ["VT-LEO-AI-<NNN>"]

  specification:
    title: "<Human-readable title>"
    description: |
      <What this software item does and why it exists>
    acceptance_criteria:
      - criterion: "<Name>"
        type: "functional"   # functional | safety | performance
        measurement: "Test"
        target: "<Measurable pass condition>"

  implementation:
    artifacts:
      - artifact_type: "source_code"
        location: "<relative/path/to/file>"
        description: "<Key function or class names>"
        storage_location: "git"
    technical_details:
      language: "Python"
      loc: 0
      key_functions: ["<function_name>"]

  safety_characteristics:
    safety_class: "B"   # A | B | C
    safety_critical_functions:
      - "<Any safety-relevant behaviour this module is responsible for>"
    risk_control_measures:
      - "<How risk is controlled in this implementation>"

  verification_status:
    verification_method: "Test"
    verification_complete: false
```

