## Risk YAML Schema (minimum required fields)

```yaml
# -- R-LEO-AI-<NNN> -- <Short title>
# ISO 14971 / IEC 62304 Risk

- id: "R-LEO-AI-<NNN>"
  title: "<One-sentence description of the risk>"

  hazard:
    description: >
      <What could go wrong — the hazardous condition>
    category: "clinical_safety"   # clinical_safety | data_protection | usability | security | availability

  hazardous_situation: >
    <The sequence of events that leads from the hazard to harm>

  harm:
    description: >
      <What harm occurs to the patient, user, or organisation>
    severity: "serious"   # negligible | minor | serious | critical | catastrophic

  initial_risk_estimate:
    severity: 3        # 1-5
    probability: 2     # 1-5
    detectability: 3   # 1-5
    rpn: 18            # severity * probability * detectability
    risk_level: "medium"   # low | medium | high | critical

  mitigation_measures:
    - control_type: "protective_measure"   # protective_measure | design_feature | procedural_control | information_for_safety
      description: >
        <What the control does>
      implemented_by: ["DI-LEO-AI-<NNN>"]
      verified_by: ["VT-LEO-AI-<NNN>"]
      effectiveness: "effective"   # effective | partially_effective | pending

  residual_risk_estimate:
    severity: 2
    probability: 1
    detectability: 3
    rpn: 6
    risk_level: "low"
    acceptability: "acceptable"   # acceptable | conditionally_acceptable | unacceptable
    justification: >
      <Why the residual risk is acceptable>

  monitoring:
    monitoring_plan: >
      <How this risk will be monitored post-deployment>
    metrics:
      - "<Measurable metric>"
    review_frequency: "Quarterly"

  metadata:
    identified_by: "<Source — threat model ID, incident, design review>"
    identified_date: "<YYYY-MM-DD>"
    status: "analyzed"   # identified | analyzed | mitigated | closed
    tags:
      - "<feature-area>"
```

